# L §4.2: "A calendar's coverage is the span of the row that states it; a day outside it is a hole naming the
# calendar and the year (HOLE-CALENDAR)", question "calendar <c> doesn't cover <year>" (L §8.1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])

ask q1: is_business(2027-03-01, len)
=== expect
q1: ?"calendar len doesn't cover 2027" (len)
  cut 2026-12-31
